{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they said, the Elohim of the Hebrews.</b> You said, 'I do not know YHWH' — that One of whom we said, the Elohim of the Hebrews. The Elohim of their fathers, and He has a claim upon them, for He is their Elohim and they are His servants and His people." "<b>Lest He encounter us.</b> Me and you. Me, if I neglect His commandment, and you, if you press us — you will suffer greater loss. Another interpretation: <b>lest He encounter us</b> — ourselves alone, so you would lose everything. Better for you that we go and return than that we die and lose everything." "<b>By plague or by sword.</b> Here Moses fulfilled the command of HaShem to warn Pharaoh first with the plague of the firstborn, as Rashi explained regarding 'Behold, I will kill your son, your firstborn.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:34.321212423Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}